s1-4-p4 : Block
s1-4-p4 = prose (cons "Conventions, conversational implicature, and coordinated language use have established accounts in Lewis, Grice, and Clark ([48](#ref-48), [49](#ref-49), [50](#ref-50)); Harnad identifies the problem of grounding symbolic expressions in their interaction with the world ([51](#ref-51)). The reception relation in §1 specifies a changing interpreter and its causal history; it is not a derivation of a full theory of natural language from a single relation. The propositions-as-types correspondence connects logical inference with typed programs ([52](#ref-52)); the cubical operations of §§3–4 extend that setting with computational identity and transport. Cybernetics and control theory have long treated the observer and controller as participants in a changing system (Wiener and Ashby, [53](#ref-53), [54](#ref-54)); Maturana and Varela develop a related account of living organization and cognition ([71](#ref-71)). These works supply concrete accounts of communication, control, and living organization whose particular definitions can be examined in the same language. Their individual results are not premises for the meaning of a represented program." nil)
